# Prose that is allowed to appear in two files. See
# DEVELOPERS.md#1-one-topic-one-place for when an entry here is the right
# answer, which is seldom.
#
# One paragraph per allowance: the files it covers, one per line, then the
# passage. Naming them is what makes it deliberate -- a copy in a file not on
# the list is news whatever those on it agreed -- and an allowance nothing
# matches is reported, so the baseline cannot outlive the repetition it
# recorded. A path line has no space in it; that is what tells the two apart.
#
# Keep it short. A long list is the checker being wrong, not the code.

# The label on `forgetAudio`, `forgetDetector`, `forgetLabelCache` and
# `forgetOutbox`: four one-line JSDoc comments on four instances of one idiom,
# a module-level singleton with a reset only a test calls. It is a label
# rather than an explanation -- there is nothing here that could live in one
# place and be linked from the others, and writing it four different ways
# would say the four exports differ when the whole point is that they do not.
# It runs to exactly twelve words, which is the only reason the checker sees
# it at all. A fifth joins the list below rather than costing four more
# entries.

frontend/src/batch/outbox.ts
frontend/src/scan/confirm.ts
frontend/src/scan/decoder.ts
frontend/src/scan/labelCache.ts
Lets a test start again from nothing. Not used by the app.

# The header and the telemetry comment shared by wsgi.py and asgi.py. Django
# specifies both modules and they differ in one word; the shape is the
# framework's, not a choice this project made, and the comment is a pointer to
# `inventory_tng.telemetry` rather than an explanation that could live in one
# place. Writing the two differently would suggest the entry points differ in
# some way that matters, which is the opposite of true.

backend/src/inventory_tng/asgi.py
backend/src/inventory_tng/wsgi.py
entry point in the shape django documents cite here rather than in an app's hook for the reasons on it does nothing when no collector is configured

# The generated stylesheet opens with the preamble its generator holds as a
# constant, because that is the only place a reader who opens the CSS will
# look. Linking is not available -- a CSS comment cannot be a link, and the
# whole purpose of the text is to be read by somebody who has just opened the
# wrong file. It is one string in one place in the source, `PREAMBLE`, and the
# copy in the artifact is written by the generator rather than typed by a
# person, so the two cannot drift.

backend/src/inventory/static/accounts/theme.css
frontend/scripts/theme-css.ts
GENERATED FILE -- DO NOT EDIT. The application's MUI theme, resolved into CSS
custom properties so that Django's /accounts/ pages are styled from the same
values the app is. Editing this by hand is undone by the next person who runs:
cd frontend && npm run theme:css Change frontend/src/theme.ts instead.
frontend/scripts/theme-css.ts says why this arrangement rather than a symlink
or a hand-written copy.
